{"course": {"schema_version": "1.0", "course_id": "mitocw-wgs-645-fall-2005", "institution": "Massachusetts Institute of Technology", "platform": "MIT OpenCourseWare", "course_codes": ["WGS.645"], "cross_listed_codes": [], "course_title": "Issues of Representation: Women, Representation, and Music in Selected Folk Traditions of the British Isles and North America", "course_slug": "wgs-645-issues-of-representation-women-representation-and-music-in-selected-folk-traditions-of-the-british-isles-and-north-america-fall-2005", "term": "Fall", "year": 2005, "as_taught_in": "Fall 2005", "language": "en", "departments": ["Women's and Gender Studies"], "academic_levels": ["Graduate"], "instructors": ["Prof. Judith Tick", "Prof. Ruth Perry"], "subject_primary": "Music", "subject_secondary": ["Music History", "Social Science", "Anthropology", "Cultural Anthropology", "Society", "Gender Studies", "Women's Studies"], "topic_tree": [{"name": "Fine Arts", "subtopics": [{"name": "Music", "specialties": ["Music History"]}]}, {"name": "Social Science", "subtopics": [{"name": "Anthropology", "specialties": ["Cultural Anthropology"]}]}, {"name": "Society", "subtopics": [{"name": "Gender Studies", "specialties": []}, {"name": "Women's Studies", "specialties": []}]}], "topic_keywords": [], "pedagogy_tags": [], "assessment_types": [], "course_feature_tags": ["Written Assignments"], "description": "This subject investigates the special relation of women to several musical folk traditions in the British Isles and North America. Throughout, we will be examining the implications of gender in the creation, transmission, and performance of music. Because virtually all societies operate to some extent on a gendered division of labor (and of expressive roles) the music of these societies is marked by the gendering of musical repertoires, traditions of instrumentation, performance settings, and styles. This seminar will examine the gendered dimensions of the music - the song texts, the performance 